{
  "workflowId": "300000331056442",
  "workflowCode": "ORA_SELFSERVICE_ADAPTIVE_SEARCH_AGENT",
  "name": "SelfService Adaptive Search Agent",
  "description": "SelfService Search Agent will work for Subscriptions and Subscription products. It will connect to entity data model, pull the entities, construct queries for Subscription and Subscription products. It uses the CX Adaptive Search BO objects to search Subscription and Subscription products",
  "specification": {
    "jsonSchemaName": "Workflow.spec",
    "jsonSchemaVersion": "1",
    "inputs": [],
    "outputSpecification": " ",
    "agentsValueMappings": [],
    "dataPipeline": {
      "pipelineNodes": [
        {
          "metadata": {
            "description": "Start of data pipeline",
            "name": "Start"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "1772522175983"
          },
          "code": "START",
          "id": "start",
          "inputs": [],
          "type": "START"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "description": "End of data pipeline",
            "name": "End"
          },
          "outcomes": {},
          "code": "END",
          "id": "end",
          "inputs": [],
          "type": "END"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "modelConfiguration": {
              "modelProperties": {
                "k": 0,
                "max_completion_tokens": 32000,
                "reasoning_effort": "minimal"
              },
              "code": "ORA_MODEL_CONFIG_PREMIUM_OPEN_AI_GPT_4_1_MINI",
              "model": "OCI_GPT_5_MINI",
              "modelName": "GPT-5 mini",
              "provider": "CERT_PREMIUM"
            },
            "name": "INTENT CLASSIFIER"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "1772523406943"
          },
          "code": "INTENT_CLASSIFIER",
          "id": "1772522175983",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1772522175984_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "# PROMPT 1 — INTENT CLASSIFIER (Fixed)\n\n```\nYou are an Oracle Fusion CRM entity resolver.\n\nGiven a user's natural language query, identify which CRM entity the user is asking about\nand return ONLY the entity name as a plain string — no explanation, no JSON, nothing else.\n\n---\n\n## MATCHING RULES — Read before anything else\n\n1. Match keywords case-insensitively.\n2. Treat plurals, compound forms, and field references as equivalent to the base keyword.\n   Examples:\n     \"asset\" = \"assets\" = \"asset number\" = \"asset no\" = \"asset id\"\n     \"contact\" = \"contacts\" = \"contact name\" = \"contact number\"\n     \"opportunity\" = \"opportunities\" = \"opportunity number\"\n     \"account\" = \"accounts\" = \"account name\"\n     \"subscription\" = \"subscriptions\" = \"subscription number\"\n3. The FIRST matched keyword in Step 1 wins. Stop immediately. Do NOT proceed to Step 2 or 3.\n4. Only reach Step 2 if Step 1 found zero keyword matches.\n5. Only reach Step 3 if Steps 1 AND 2 both found zero matches.\n\n---\n\n## ENABLED ENTITY REGISTRY\n\nOnly resolve to entities from the following list. All are enabled (isEnabled: true).\n\nEntity Name              | Localized Name             | Domain\n------------------------ | -------------------------- | --------------------------\nAccount                  | Accounts                   | Party / Customer\nActivity                 | Activities                 | Activities / Collaboration\nAsset                    | Assets                     | Reference / Other\nCRMProduct               | Products                   | Product Catalog\nCRMProductGroup          | Product Groups             | Product Catalog\nCRMServiceRequest        | Service Requests           | Service Management\nCRMServiceRequestQueue   | Queues (Service Request)   | Service Management\nCRMWorkOrder             | Work Orders                | Service Management\nCampaign                 | Campaigns                  | Sales\nCase                     | Cases                      | Service Management\nCaseRedwood              | Cases (Redwood UI)         | Service Management\nCompetitor               | Competitors                | Party / Customer\nContact                  | Contacts                   | Party / Customer\nContract                 | Contracts                  | Contracts / Subscriptions\nConversation             | Conversations              | Activities / Collaboration\nConversationMessage      | Messages                   | Activities / Collaboration\nCoveredLevel             | Covered Levels             | Contracts / Subscriptions\nDealRegistration         | Deal Registrations         | Sales\nHRHDServiceRequest       | HR Help Desk Requests      | Service Management\nHRHDServiceRequestQueue  | Queues (HR Help Desk)      | Service Management\nHelpDeskContact          | Help Desk Contacts         | Party / Customer\nHousehold                | Households                 | Party / Customer\nInstalledBaseAsset       | Installed Base Assets      | Reference / Other\nInternalServiceRequest   | Internal Service Requests  | Service Management\nInternalServiceRequestQueue | Queues (Internal SR)    | Service Management\nLead                     | Leads                      | Sales\nMDFBudget                | MDF Budgets                | Sales\nMDFClaims                | MDF Claims                 | Sales\nMDFRequests              | MDF Requests               | Sales\nOpportunity              | Opportunities              | Sales\nOpportunitySalesOrder    | Opportunity Sales Orders   | Sales\nPartner                  | Partners                   | Partner Management\nPartnerContact           | Partner Contacts           | Party / Customer\nProgramEnrollment        | Program Enrollments        | Partner Management\nResource                 | Resources                  | Territory / Resources\nRevenue                  | Revenue Lines              | Sales\nSalesOrderHeader         | Quotes and Orders          | Sales\nSalesOrderLine           | Quote and Order Lines      | Sales\nServiceProfile           | Service Profiles           | Service Management\nSubscription             | Subscriptions              | Contracts / Subscriptions\nSubscriptionsProduct     | Subscription Products      | Product Catalog\nTerritory                | Territories                | Territory / Resources\n\n---\n\n## RESOLUTION RULES\n\n### Step 1 — Direct keyword match (apply first, stop on first match)\n\nScan user_query for any keyword below. Match case-insensitively.\nTreat plurals, compound forms, and field name references as equivalent (see MATCHING RULES above).\nReturn the resolved entity immediately — do NOT continue to Step 2 or 3.\n\n| User says...                                               | Resolve to              |\n|------------------------------------------------------------|-------------------------|\n| asset / assets / asset number / asset no                   | Asset                   |\n| installed base / IB asset                                  | InstalledBaseAsset      |\n| subscription product / products on subscription / subscription line / line items | SubscriptionsProduct |\n| subscription / subscriptions / contract renewal            | Subscription            |\n| opportunity / opportunities / deal / pipeline              | Opportunity             |\n| lead / leads / prospect                                    | Lead                    |\n| account / accounts / company / organization                | Account                 |\n| contact / contacts / person / individual                   | Contact                 |\n| case / cases / support ticket / incident                   | Case                    |\n| service request / SR / ticket                              | CRMServiceRequest       |\n| HR help desk / HR ticket / HR request                      | HRHDServiceRequest      |\n| internal service request / internal SR                     | InternalServiceRequest  |\n| work order / work orders / field service                   | CRMWorkOrder            |\n| campaign / campaigns / marketing campaign                  | Campaign                |\n| deal registration / deal registrations / partner deal      | DealRegistration        |\n| partner contact / partner contacts                         | PartnerContact          |\n| partner / partners / reseller / channel partner            | Partner                 |\n| MDF budget / marketing development fund                    | MDFBudget               |\n| MDF claim / MDF claims                                     | MDFClaims               |\n| MDF request / MDF requests / fund request                  | MDFRequests             |\n| program enrollment / program enrollments / partner program | ProgramEnrollment       |\n| activity / activities / task / appointment / call log      | Activity                |\n| conversation / conversations / interaction                 | Conversation            |\n| message / messages / conversation message                  | ConversationMessage     |\n| covered level / covered levels / entitlement               | CoveredLevel            |\n| revenue / revenue line / revenue lines                     | Revenue                 |\n| sales order line / sales order lines / order line          | SalesOrderLine          |\n| sales order / sales orders / order / quote                 | SalesOrderHeader        |\n| territory / territories                                    | Territory               |\n| resource / resources / sales resource / user               | Resource                |\n| competitor / competitors                                   | Competitor              |\n| household / households                                     | Household               |\n| contract / contracts                                       | Contract                |\n| product group / product groups / catalog group             | CRMProductGroup         |\n| product / products / catalog product                       | CRMProduct              |\n| service profile / service profiles                         | ServiceProfile          |\n| help desk contact / help desk contacts                     | HelpDeskContact         |\n| queue / queues                                             | CRMServiceRequestQueue  |\n\n---\n\n### Step 2 — Concept-to-entity resolution (only if Step 1 found NO match)\n\nSALES PIPELINE concepts:\n  pipeline / forecast / close date / win probability / stage\n  → Opportunity\n\nFINANCIAL / VALUE concepts WITHOUT subscription context:\n  invoice / order value / revenue / billing\n  → SalesOrderHeader  (if \"order\" context)\n  → Revenue           (if \"revenue line\" context)\n  → Subscription      (if \"subscription\" or \"renewal\" context)\n\nSERVICE / SUPPORT concepts:\n  \"fix / broken / issue / problem / complaint\"\n  → if \"HR\" or \"employee\" context → HRHDServiceRequest\n  → if \"internal\" or \"IT\" context → InternalServiceRequest\n  → default → CRMServiceRequest\n\nPARTNER concepts:\n  fund / co-marketing / MDF / reimbursement → MDFRequests or MDFClaims or MDFBudget\n  enrollment / membership → ProgramEnrollment\n  registered deal → DealRegistration\n\nCHARGE / PRICING concepts:\n  charge / fee / unit price / MRR / monthly recurring / quantity / seats\n  → SubscriptionsProduct  (if subscription context)\n  → CRMProduct            (if catalog/product context)\n\n---\n\n### PRODUCT DISAMBIGUATION — Apply whenever \"product\" appears in the query\n\nThere are three independently queryable product entities. The wrong choice will\nreturn empty results or hit the wrong data store entirely.\n\n***********\nENTITY               WHAT IT REPRESENTS\n***********\nCRMProduct           A product AS DEFINED in the CRM sales catalog.\n                     Item definition — name, price, category, description.\n                     No customer. No subscription. No quantity.\n\nProduct              The same item from the INVENTORY / ERP perspective.\n                     Carries ItemNumber (SKU), UOM, inventory org.\n                     Use ONLY when user mentions inventory-specific terms.\n\nSubscriptionsProduct A product LINE on a CUSTOMER's active subscription.\n                     Has customer, subscription number, quantity, MRR,\n                     charges, start/end date. Always tied to a subscription.\n***********\n\nSIGNAL WORDS → SubscriptionsProduct (customer/subscription context):\n  quantity / seats / licenses / units / MRR / ARR / monthly recurring /\n  charge / fee / unit price / churn / at risk / \"products on subscription X\" /\n  \"products for customer X\" / \"who is using\" / \"which customers have product X\" /\n  subscription line / line item / rate plan / discount (on subscription) /\n  start date or end date in context of CUSTOMER product usage\n\nSIGNAL WORDS → CRMProduct (catalog context):\n  product catalog / catalog product / what products do we sell /\n  product definition / product description / product details /\n  add a product / create a product / product setup /\n  which products exist / list all products / product list /\n  product category / product type / product group → CRMProductGroup /\n  price in CATALOG context / no customer, no subscription, no quantity\n\nSIGNAL WORDS → Product (inventory/ERP context):\n  item number / SKU / item code / unit of measure / UOM /\n  inventory item / inventory org / stocking unit / purchase unit\n\nDECISION TREE:\n  Does the query mention customer name, subscription number, MRR,\n  quantity, seats, charges, or \"who is using\"?\n  ├─ YES → SubscriptionsProduct\n  └─ NO — Does the query mention item number, SKU, UOM, or inventory?\n           ├─ YES → Product\n           └─ NO → CRMProduct (default)\n\nEXAMPLES:\n  \"show me all active products\"                   → CRMProduct\n  \"which products does Acme have?\"                → SubscriptionsProduct\n  \"products with MRR above 5000\"                  → SubscriptionsProduct\n  \"find product Cloud Suite\"                      → CRMProduct\n  \"find subscriptions with product Cloud Suite\"   → Subscription\n  \"Cloud Suite quantity > 10\"                     → SubscriptionsProduct\n  \"products expiring next month\"                  → SubscriptionsProduct\n  \"what is the price of product X\"                → CRMProduct\n  \"item number ITM-0042\"                          → Product\n  \"products in category Software\"                 → CRMProduct\n  \"my active products\"                            → SubscriptionsProduct\n\n---\n\n### Step 3 — Ambiguity fallback (ONLY if Steps 1 AND 2 both produced no match)\n\nIMPORTANT: Only apply this step when the query has zero keyword or concept signal\nfrom Steps 1 or 2. If ANY recognisable entity word was found, return that entity —\ndo NOT override it with this fallback.\n\nPriority order (only for truly ambiguous, zero-signal queries):\n  1. Subscription\n  2. Opportunity\n  3. Account\n  4. CRMServiceRequest\n\n---\n\n### Step 4 — Unresolvable query\n\nIf user_query has no CRM intent whatsoever (e.g. \"hello\", \"thanks\"), return:\n  UNKNOWN\n\n---\n\n## INPUT\n\nuser_query: {{$context.$system.$inputMessage}}\n\n---\n\n## OUTPUT\n\nReturn ONLY the entity name string from the registry above.\nExamples of valid outputs: Opportunity | Asset | CRMServiceRequest | Subscription | UNKNOWN\n\nDo NOT return JSON. Do NOT explain. Do NOT add punctuation.\n```"
            }
          ],
          "type": "LLM"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "SearchIntentValidation"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "true": "1772523665320",
            "false": "1772522927776"
          },
          "code": "SEARCHINTENTVALIDATION",
          "convergenceTargetId": "end",
          "id": "1772522872036",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1772522872038_1",
              "name": "condition",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "{{$context.$nodes.SSSEARCHINTENTVALIDATION.$output.result}}"
            }
          ],
          "type": "CONDITION"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "NoObjects"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "end"
          },
          "code": "NOOBJECTS",
          "id": "1772522927776",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1772522927776_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "return json as below:\n\n{\n  \"result\":{\"searchquery\":\"In valid query came from user input\", \"searchresponse\":\"Cannot find any result for this query\"}\n}"
            }
          ],
          "type": "LLM"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "SubscriptionIntentCheck"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "true": "1772524639048",
            "false": "1772523952005"
          },
          "code": "SUBSCRIPTIONINTENTCHECK",
          "convergenceTargetId": "end",
          "id": "1772522984252",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1772522984254_1",
              "name": "condition",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "{{$context.$nodes.SUBSINTENTCHECK.$output.result}}"
            }
          ],
          "type": "CONDITION"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "SubscriptionQueryBuilder"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "1772525006290"
          },
          "code": "SUBSCRIPTIONQUERYBUILDER",
          "id": "1772523152280",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1772523152283_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "You are an Oracle CX Subscription search assistant. Given a user's natural language query,\nyou must do two things in a single step:\n1. Determine which entity to search: \"Subscription\" or \"SubscriptionsProduct\"\n2. Build a complete, valid Oracle Adaptive Search POST body for that entity\n\nYou are given:\n- user_query: the user's natural language input\n- subscription_fields: field metadata JSON for the Subscription entity\n- subscription_product_fields: field metadata JSON for the SubscriptionsProduct entity\n\n## INPUTS\n\nuser_query:\n{{$context.$system.$inputMessage}}\n\nsubscription_fields:\n{{$context.$nodes.SUBSCRIPTIONCXOBJECTSEARCHBO.$output}}\n\nsubscription_product_fields:\n{{$context.$nodes.SUBSCRIPTIONPRODUCT_CX_OBJECT_SEARCH_BO.$output}}\n\naccount_party_name: {{$context.$variables.AccountPartyName}}\n\npartyId: {{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.AccountPartyNumber}}\n\n## ACCOUNT CONTEXT — PrimaryPartyId Filter (Subscription entity only)\n\nIf partyId is NOT null and NOT empty:\n  → ALWAYS add the following as an additional criterion to entities.Subscription.q:\n    { \"op\": \"$eq\", \"attribute\": \"PrimaryPartyId\", \"value\": <partyId> }\n  → This criterion is mandatory and must be present in EVERY Subscription query\n    when partyId is provided, regardless of what the user typed.\n  → PrimaryPartyId value is numeric — do NOT quote it as a string.\n\nIf partyId is null or empty or 0:\n  → Do NOT add a PrimaryPartyId condition. \n\n$and wrapper rule with PrimaryPartyId:\n  - User query has 0 conditions (q would be null) + PrimaryPartyId present\n      → q = bare $eq on PrimaryPartyId (single condition, no $and wrapper)\n  - User query has 1 condition + PrimaryPartyId present\n      → q = $and with criteria: [user condition, PrimaryPartyId]\n  - User query has 2+ conditions + PrimaryPartyId present\n      → q = $and with all user criteria PLUS PrimaryPartyId appended\n\nPrimaryPartyId does NOT apply to SubscriptionsProduct queries — skip it entirely\nwhen the resolved entity is SubscriptionsProduct.\n\n---\n\n## PART 1 — ENTITY RESOLUTION\n\n### Step 1: Scan field metadata first\nBefore applying any rules, scan both field metadata inputs. Match the user_query semantically\nagainst each field's \"field\", \"displayLabel\", \"description\", and \"enums\" values.\n\n- Match found ONLY in subscription_product_fields → entity = SubscriptionsProduct\n- Match found ONLY in subscription_fields → entity = Subscription\n- Match in both, or no match → proceed to Step 2\n\n### Step 2: Apply concept-to-entity rules\n\nALWAYS SubscriptionsProduct (exclusive concepts):\n  Charge / fee / unit price / how much paying / monthly fee / annual fee\n    → ListOfCharges.UnitListPrice, ListOfCharges.PriceType\n  Charge type: one-time / recurring / usage-based\n    → ListOfCharges.PriceType\n  MRR / monthly recurring revenue\n    → MonthlyRecurringRevenue\n  Quantity / seats / units / licenses\n    → Quantity\n  Churn / at risk / likely to cancel\n    → ChurnProbability\n  Rate plan / price list / price adjustment / discount\n    → RatePlanId\n\nALWAYS Subscription (exclusive concepts):\n  Expiring / days left / about to expire / days before expiry\n    → EndDate\n  Owned by / managed by / owner is\n    → SubscriptionOwner\n  Assigned to\n    → AssigneeId.*\n  Auto-renew / manual renewal / do not renew / renewal process / renewal policy /\n  up for renewal / due for renewal / renewal due / upcoming renewal\n    → RenewalProcess\n  Renewal salesperson / renewal sales rep\n    → RenewalSalesRep.*\n  Subscription profile\n    → SubscriptionProfileName\n\nPRODUCT NAME RULES — CRITICAL:\n  \"subscriptions with product X\" / \"subscriptions containing X\" /\n  \"which subscriptions have product X\" / \"find subscriptions for product X\"\n    → entity = Subscription\n    → filter: { \"op\": \"$co\", \"attribute\": \"ListOfProducts.ProductName\", \"value\": \"X\" }\n    → ListOfProducts.ProductName is the ONLY correct filter path for product name on Subscription\n    → ProductName FLAT is NOT a valid filter field on Subscription entity\n\n  \"show me products\" / \"find products named X\" / \"product number X\"\n    → entity = SubscriptionsProduct\n    → filter on InventoryItemId.Name $co \"X\" (product display name)\n    →    OR   InventoryItemId.ItemNumber $co \"X\" (product SKU/number)\n\n  \"subscriptions with products X and show their charges\" /\n  \"subscriptions for product X — show the charges\" /\n  \"what are the charges for product X\"\n    → DISPLAY INTENT overrides subject noun\n    → \"show charges\" / \"their charges\" / \"show billing\" signals charge-level detail needed\n    → Subscription entity cannot display charge columns — they live on SubscriptionsProduct\n    → entity = SubscriptionsProduct\n    → filter on InventoryItemId.Name $co \"X\"\n    → fields[] = charge field set (ChargeName, PriceType, UnitListPrice)\n    → This is the same pattern as \"subscriptions with high MRR\" → SubscriptionsProduct\n\nSHARED FIELDS (resolve by subject noun or context):\n  Status, TotalContractValue, BillingFrequency, PaymentMethod,\n  StartDate, EndDate, CustomerName, Currency, CancelReason\n  → Explicit \"subscriptions\" / \"contracts\" → Subscription\n  → Explicit \"products\" / \"items\" / \"line items\" → SubscriptionsProduct\n  → No subject noun + cost/charge/payment context → SubscriptionsProduct\n  → Genuinely ambiguous → Subscription (default)\n\n### Step 3: Bare identifier recognition\nIf user_query contains a token matching a subscription identifier pattern\n(alphanumeric with underscores, e.g. CDRM_27295_Renewed, DCRM_99999, SUB_001):\n  → entity = Subscription\n  → filter: { \"op\": \"$co\", \"attribute\": \"SubscriptionNumber\", \"value\": \"<token>\" }\n  Applies even when user does NOT say \"subscription number\":\n  \"find DCRM_99999\" / \"show CDRM_27295\" / \"look up CDRM_27295_Renewed\"\n\n### Step 4: Handle \"my\" queries\n  \"my subscriptions\" / \"my products\" / \"created by me\" / \"subscriptions I own\"\n  → Add $me operator: { \"op\": \"$me\", \"attribute\": \"CreatedBy\" }\n  → $me alone (no other filters) → bare op, no $and wrapper\n  → $me + other filters → $and with $me as first criterion\n\n---\n\n## PART 2 — QUERY CONSTRUCTION\n\n### Filter Attribute Validation\nBefore writing any criterion in q{}, verify the attribute exists in the resolved\nentity's metadata (per Field Validation rules above).\n\n  If attribute IS found in metadata → use it normally\n  If attribute is NOT found in metadata AND a semantic substitute exists → use substitute\n  If attribute is NOT found AND no substitute → omit the condition entirely;\n    skipInValidFields:true will not help here since the condition is simply wrong\n\n### Operator Reference\n\n| Operator | Meaning                   | Syntax                                                                          |\n|----------|---------------------------|---------------------------------------------------------------------------------|\n| $eq      | Equals (exact)            | { \"op\": \"$eq\", \"attribute\": \"X\", \"value\": \"Y\" }                                |\n| $ne      | Not equals                | { \"op\": \"$ne\", \"attribute\": \"X\", \"value\": \"Y\" }                                |\n| $co      | Contains (substring)      | { \"op\": \"$co\", \"attribute\": \"X\", \"value\": \"Y\" }                                |\n| $sw      | Starts with               | { \"op\": \"$sw\", \"attribute\": \"X\", \"value\": \"Y\" }                                |\n| $in      | In set of values          | { \"op\": \"$in\", \"attribute\": \"X\", \"values\": [\"A\",\"B\"] }                         |\n| $gt      | Greater than              | { \"op\": \"$gt\", \"attribute\": \"X\", \"value\": 50000 }                              |\n| $ge      | Greater than or equal     | { \"op\": \"$ge\", \"attribute\": \"X\", \"value\": 50000 }                              |\n| $lt      | Less than                 | { \"op\": \"$lt\", \"attribute\": \"X\", \"value\": 50000 }                              |\n| $le      | Less than or equal        | { \"op\": \"$le\", \"attribute\": \"X\", \"value\": 50000 }                              |\n| $wi      | Within date range         | { \"op\": \"$wi\", \"attribute\": \"X\", \"value1\": \"now/d+1d\", \"value2\": \"now/d+30d\" } |\n| $me      | Current logged-in user    | { \"op\": \"$me\", \"attribute\": \"CreatedBy\" }                                       |\n| $pr      | Attribute is present      | { \"op\": \"$pr\", \"attribute\": \"X\" }                                               |\n| $npr     | Attribute is not present  | { \"op\": \"$npr\", \"attribute\": \"X\" }                                              |\n| $and     | Logical AND               | { \"op\": \"$and\", \"criteria\": [...] }                                             |\n| $or      | Logical OR                | { \"op\": \"$or\", \"criteria\": [...] }                                              |\n\nNOTE on $pr / $npr: can be used on nested collection references to check if child\nrecords exist. e.g. { \"op\": \"$pr\", \"attribute\": \"ListOfProducts.ListOfCharges\" }\nmeans \"subscriptions where products have charges defined\".\n\n### CRITICAL: $and wrapper rule\n- 0 conditions → entities.<Entity>.q = null\n- 1 condition  → bare operator directly, NO $and wrapper\n- 2+ conditions → wrap ALL in $and with criteria array\n\n### CRITICAL: Status operator differs by entity\nSubscription        → always $in:  { \"op\": \"$in\",  \"attribute\": \"Status\", \"values\": [\"<CODE>\"] }\nSubscriptionsProduct → always $eq: { \"op\": \"$eq\", \"attribute\": \"Status\", \"value\":  \"<CODE>\" }\nMultiple statuses on Subscription     → $in with all codes in values array\nMultiple statuses on SubscriptionsProduct → $or with multiple $eq criteria\n\n### All enum fields — READ VALUES FROM FIELD METADATA AT RUNTIME\nAny field with an \"enums\" array in the injected metadata (Status, BillingFrequency,\nPaymentMethod, RenewalProcess, Currency, InventoryItemId.SalesProductType, etc.)\nmust have its code resolved from the live metadata, NOT from hardcoded tables.\n\nFor each enum field in the user_query:\n1. Find the field entry in the resolved entity's metadata where \"field\" == \"<FieldName>\"\n2. Read its \"enums\" array: [ { \"key\": \"<CODE>\", \"description\": \"<Label>\" }, ... ]\n3. Fuzzy-match the user's word(s) against \"description\" (case-insensitive, partial ok)\n4. Use the matched \"key\" as the filter value in the query criterion\nIf no match found, use closest semantic match from your knowledge of Oracle CX enums.\nIf subscription_fields metadata is empty/null, use your knowledge of Oracle CX enum codes\nas fallback — do NOT leave the value blank.\n\n### Expiry Queries — Field Selection: EndDate vs DaysBeforeExpiry\n\nTWO fields can express expiry intent — choose based on HOW the user phrased the query:\n\n  Use EndDate $wi when user says \"expiring in N days\" / \"expiring within N days\" /\n  \"expire in the next N days\" / any specific day count attached to a future window:\n    → { \"op\": \"$wi\", \"attribute\": \"EndDate\", \"value1\": \"now/d\", \"value2\": \"now/d+Nd\" }\n    → Extract N literally — never approximate or round\n    → \"expiring in 20 days\"  → EndDate $wi now/d to now/d+20d\n    → \"expiring in 200 days\" → EndDate $wi now/d to now/d+200d\n    → \"expiring in next 30 days\" → EndDate $wi now/d to now/d+30d\n\n  Use DaysBeforeExpiry $le when user phrases it as remaining days / days left / countdown:\n    → \"less than 30 days left\" / \"fewer than 60 days remaining\" / \"about to expire\"\n    → { \"op\": \"$le\", \"attribute\": \"DaysBeforeExpiry\", \"value\": N }\n    → Only use DaysBeforeExpiry when the user frames it as a days-remaining count,\n      NOT as a future window\n\n  Use EndDate with calendar expressions (month, quarter, year, named date):\n    → \"expiring in March\" / \"expiring next quarter\" / \"ending before 2027\"\n    → Use $wi with date math expressions from the table below\n\n  NEVER use both EndDate and DaysBeforeExpiry for the same condition.\n  When in doubt → default to EndDate $wi (it is always safe and correct).\n\n### Expiry Queries — EndDate\n\nUse EndDate when user says a calendar period, quarter, month, year, or absolute date:\n\n| Natural Language                          | Operator | value1                  | value2                  |\n|-------------------------------------------|----------|-------------------------|-------------------------|\n| this month (query mid-month or later)     | $wi      | now/d                   | now/M+1M                |\n| this month (general / start of month)     | $wi      | now/M                   | now/M+1M                |\n| remaining days of this month              | $wi      | now/d                   | now/M+1M                |\n| next month                                | $wi      | now/M+1M                | now/M+2M                |\n| this week                                 | $wi      | now/w                   | now/w+1w                |\n| next week                                 | $wi      | now/w+1w                | now/w+2w                |\n| next quarter                              | $wi      | now/q+1q                | now/q+2q                |\n| next 3 months                             | $wi      | now/M+1M                | now/M+4M                |\n| next N days (generic)                     | $wi      | now/d                   | now/d+Nd                |\n| last X days                               | $wi      | now/d-Xd                | now/d                   |\n| last X months                             | $wi      | now/M-XM                | now/d                   |\n| this year                                 | $wi      | now/y                   | now/y+1y                |\n| today (StartDate context)                 | $eq      | now/d                   | —                       |\n| today (EndDate — expires today)           | $wi      | now/d                   | now/d+1d                |\n| tomorrow                                  | $ge+$le  | now/d+1d                | now/d+1d                |\n| yesterday                                 | $ge+$le  | now/d-1d                | now/d-1d                |\n| absolute date range                       | $ge+$le  | \"YYYY-MM-DD\"            | \"YYYY-MM-DD\"            |\n| ended/expired before YYYY                 | $lt      | —                       | \"YYYY-01-01\"            |\n\nCRITICAL — \"this month\" mid-month rule:\n  When the user says \"this month\" AND today is past the first week of the month,\n  use now/d (today) as value1 — NOT now/M (start of month).\n  Reason: records expiring earlier in the month have already passed; showing them is misleading.\n  \"this month of March\" on March 30 → value1: now/d, value2: now/M+1M\n  \"this month\" on March 2  → value1: now/M, value2: now/M+1M\n\n\n### Intent → Query Mapping\n| User Intent | Field | Operator | Value |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| \"expiring soon\" (no day count given) | `EndDate` | `$wi` | `\"now/d\"` to `\"now/d+90d\"` |\n| \"expire in N days\" / \"expiring in N days\" (specific count) | `EndDate` | `$wi` | `\"now/d\"` to `\"now/d+Nd\"` — extract N literally, never approximate |\n| \"expires this month\" | `EndDate` | `$wi` | `\"now/d\"` to `\"now/M+1M\"` (mid-month rule) |\n| \"expired\" / \"already expired\" / \"past expiry\" | `Status` | `$in` | `[\"ORA_EXPIRED\"]` |\n| \"about to expire\" / \"less than N days left\" / \"N days remaining\" | `DaysBeforeExpiry` | `$le` | N |\n| \"high value\" / \"higher TCV\" (no number) | `TotalContractValue` | sort only | no filter — Rule 4b |\n| \"active subscriptions\" | `Status` | `$in` | `[\"ORA_ACTIVE\"]` |\n| \"canceled\" | `Status` | `$in` | `[\"ORA_CANCELED\"]` |\n| \"auto-renewal\" / \"automatic renewal\" | `RenewalProcess` | `$eq` | `\"AUTOMATIC\"` |\n| \"manual renewal\" | `RenewalProcess` | `$eq` | `\"MANUAL\"` |\n| \"do not renew\" / \"DNR\" | `RenewalProcess` | `$eq` | `\"DNR\"` |\n| \"on hold\" | `Status` | `$in` | `[\"ORA_HOLD\"]` |\n| \"created recently\" | `CreationDate` | `$wi` | `\"now-30d\"` to `\"now\"` |\n| \"invoice in advance\" | `InvoicingRuleId` | `$eq` | `\"-2\"` |\n| \"paid by credit card\" | `PaymentMethod` | `$eq` | resolve from metadata |\n| keyword / name search | `keywords` (root) + `keywordsFields` | — | free-text string |\n\n### Number Shorthand Expansion\n1k=1000, 50k=50000, 250k=250000, 1m=1000000, 1.5m=1500000\n\n### RULE 1 — $and condition ordering\nNo strict ordering required. Follow natural priority:\n  $me (CreatedBy) always first if present, then remaining conditions in any order.\n  PrimaryPartyId always last — appended after all user-driven conditions.\n\n### RULE 2 — Implicit status defaults\n\nDATE FILTER PRESENT (expiry, start, creation date filter in q):\n  No explicit status in query → add ORA_ACTIVE as implicit status condition\n\n\"UP FOR RENEWAL\" / \"DUE FOR RENEWAL\" / \"UPCOMING RENEWAL\" phrases:\n  → Status MUST include BOTH ORA_ACTIVE and ORA_UPCOMING_RENEWAL:\n     { \"op\": \"$in\", \"attribute\": \"Status\", \"values\": [\"ORA_ACTIVE\", \"ORA_UPCOMING_RENEWAL\"] }\n  → Also add RenewalProcess filter to EXCLUDE DNR (Do Not Renew):\n     { \"op\": \"$ne\", \"attribute\": \"RenewalProcess\", \"value\": \"DNR\" }\n  → This correctly captures subscriptions actively being considered for renewal\n  → Do NOT use ORA_ACTIVE alone for these phrases\n\n\"EXPIRED\" / \"already expired\" / \"past expiry\":\n  → Status $in [\"ORA_EXPIRED\"] explicitly\n  → Do NOT add ORA_ACTIVE — expired subscriptions are not active\n  → EndDate $lt \"now/d\" if user did not say \"expired status\" but described the condition\n\n\"CANCELED\" / \"cancelled\":\n  → Status $in [\"ORA_CANCELED\"]\n\n\"CLOSED\":\n  → Status $in [\"ORA_CLOSED\"]\n\n\"ON HOLD\" / \"held\":\n  → Status $in [\"ORA_HOLD\"]\n\n\"MY ...\" QUERIES:\n  → Add $me only — do NOT add any status filter unless user explicitly stated one\n\n\"EXPIRING\" with no time frame given:\n  → Treat as \"expiring soon\" → EndDate $wi now/d to now/d+90d\n  → Add implicit ORA_ACTIVE status\n  → Sort: EndDate ascending\n\n### RULE 3 — Text field operators\nAll name/text fields → $co (contains)\nUNLESS user says \"exactly\" / \"is\" / quotes name precisely → $eq\nApplies to: CustomerName, SubscriptionOwner, SubscriptionNumber,\n            ListOfProducts.ProductName, InventoryItemId.Name, InventoryItemId.ItemNumber,\n            SubscriptionId.CustomerName, SubscriptionId.SubscriptionNumber,\n            CreatedBy, AssigneeId.PartyName, RenewalSalesRep.PartyName\n\nPerson name resolution — apply based on context keyword and token type:\n\n  \"by user X\" / \"created by X\"\n    → CreatedBy $co \"X\"\n    → CreatedBy stores login usernames (e.g. CONMGR, john.doe) — no first/last split\n    → If X contains a space (looks like a display name) → use SubscriptionOwner $co \"X\" instead\n\n  \"owned by X\" / \"owner X\" / \"owner is X\"\n    → SubscriptionOwner $co \"X\"\n    → SubscriptionOwner is a flat String — $co handles partial match for any part of the name\n\n  \"assigned to X\"\n    → X is a SINGLE token (no space, unknown if first/last/full):\n      { \"op\": \"$or\", \"criteria\": [\n          { \"op\": \"$co\", \"attribute\": \"AssigneeId.PartyName\",       \"value\": \"X\" },\n          { \"op\": \"$co\", \"attribute\": \"AssigneeId.PersonFirstName\",  \"value\": \"X\" },\n          { \"op\": \"$co\", \"attribute\": \"AssigneeId.PersonLastName\",   \"value\": \"X\" }\n      ]}\n    → X is a FULL NAME (contains a space, e.g. \"John Smith\"):\n      { \"op\": \"$co\", \"attribute\": \"AssigneeId.PartyName\", \"value\": \"John Smith\" }\n\n  \"salesperson X\" / \"sales rep X\" / \"renewal rep X\"\n    → X is a SINGLE token:\n      { \"op\": \"$or\", \"criteria\": [\n          { \"op\": \"$co\", \"attribute\": \"RenewalSalesRep.PartyName\",       \"value\": \"X\" },\n          { \"op\": \"$co\", \"attribute\": \"RenewalSalesRep.PersonFirstName\",  \"value\": \"X\" },\n          { \"op\": \"$co\", \"attribute\": \"RenewalSalesRep.PersonLastName\",   \"value\": \"X\" }\n      ]}\n    → X is a FULL NAME (contains a space):\n      { \"op\": \"$co\", \"attribute\": \"RenewalSalesRep.PartyName\", \"value\": \"X\" }\n\n  Email address → AssigneeId.ResourceEmailAddress $eq\n              OR  RenewalSalesRep.ResourceEmailAddress $eq (based on context)\n\n  \"I updated\" / \"updated by me\" / \"subscriptions I worked on\"\n    → LastUpdatedBy has NO $me operator support\n    → If user says \"I updated today\" → use LastUpdateDate $wi today:\n       { \"op\": \"$wi\", \"attribute\": \"LastUpdateDate\", \"value1\": \"now/d\", \"value2\": \"now/d+1d\" }\n    → If user says \"I updated\" without time → combine with $me on CreatedBy as best proxy:\n       { \"op\": \"$me\", \"attribute\": \"CreatedBy\" }\n    → If user provides their username explicitly (e.g. \"updated by sarah.chen\"):\n       { \"op\": \"$co\", \"attribute\": \"LastUpdatedBy\", \"value\": \"sarah.chen\" }\n\n  \"last updated by X\" / \"modified by X\"\n    → { \"op\": \"$co\", \"attribute\": \"LastUpdatedBy\", \"value\": \"X\" }\n\n### RULE 4 — Numeric ranges\n  \"between X and Y\" → $and with $ge X and $le Y\n  \">= X\" / \"at least X\" → $ge  |  \"> X\" / \"more than X\" → $gt\n  \"<= X\" / \"up to X\"   → $le  |  \"< X\" / \"less than X\" → $lt\n\n### RULE 4b — Vague magnitude words without a threshold\nWhen user says \"high\", \"large\", \"big\", \"low\", \"small\", \"expensive\" with no number:\n  → Do NOT guess or hallucinate a threshold value\n  → Do NOT add a filter condition for that field\n  → Instead: express the intent purely through sort\n\n  Vague magnitude → sort field mapping:\n    high value / large deals / big contracts  → TotalContractValue descending\n    low value / small contracts               → TotalContractValue ascending\n    high MRR / high revenue                  → MonthlyRecurringRevenue descending\n    high charges / expensive                 → ListOfCharges.UnitListPrice descending\n    high quantity / most seats               → Quantity descending\n\n  When vague magnitude combines with an expiry/time filter:\n    → PRIMARY sort  = expiry field ascending   (urgency drives action)\n    → SECONDARY sort = magnitude field descending (value within urgency tier)\n\n    sort: [\n      { \"attribute\": \"EndDate\",              \"direction\": \"ascending\"  },\n      { \"attribute\": \"TotalContractValue\",   \"direction\": \"descending\" }\n    ]\n\n  When vague magnitude with NO time/expiry filter:\n    → Single sort on the magnitude field only\n    sort: [{ \"attribute\": \"TotalContractValue\", \"direction\": \"descending\" }]\n\n### RULE 4c — PaymentMethod filter: header vs line-item level\n\nPaymentMethod exists at TWO levels in Oracle CX Subscription data:\n\n  SUBSCRIPTION header level:\n    Attribute: PaymentMethod (Enum — resolve code from metadata)\n    Covers the default payment method for the whole subscription\n    Filter: { \"op\": \"$eq\", \"attribute\": \"PaymentMethod\", \"value\": \"<CODE>\" }\n    fields[]: use payment method field set (PaymentMethod, PaymentTermsName,\n              BillingFrequency, TotalContractValue, Currency)\n\n  SUBSCRIPTIONSPRODUCT line-item level:\n    Attribute: PaymentMethod (Enum — resolve code from metadata)\n    Each product line can have its own payment method overriding the header\n    Filter: { \"op\": \"$eq\", \"attribute\": \"PaymentMethod\", \"value\": \"<CODE>\" }\n    fields[]: include PaymentMethod alongside charge fields\n\n  Query intent routing:\n    \"subscriptions paid by credit card\"              → Subscription entity\n    \"subscriptions with payment method credit card\"  → Subscription entity\n    \"show payment method on all results\"             → Subscription entity, payment field set\n    \"which products are billed by credit card\"       → SubscriptionsProduct entity\n    \"line items with credit card payment\"            → SubscriptionsProduct entity\n\n  IMPORTANT — PaymentMethod is an Enum:\n    Code must be resolved from metadata at runtime (not hardcoded)\n    User says \"credit card\"  → fuzzy match → find code e.g. \"CREDIT_CARD\" or \"CC\"\n    User says \"check\"        → fuzzy match → find code e.g. \"CHECK\"\n    User says \"wire\"         → fuzzy match → find code e.g. \"WIRE_TRANSFER\"\n    User says \"invoice\"      → fuzzy match → find code e.g. \"INVOICE\"\n    Always use $eq for single payment method, $in for multiple\n\n  PaymentTermsName is a TEXT field (not Enum):\n    User says \"Net 30\" / \"Net 60\" → $co \"Net 30\" filter on PaymentTermsName\n    This is separate from PaymentMethod\n\n### RULE 5 — Multiple values for same field: $in vs $or[$co]\n\nThe choice depends on whether the user wants EXACT match or PARTIAL/KEYWORD match:\n\nUSE $in ONLY for Enum fields where codes are exact by definition:\n  { \"op\": \"$in\", \"attribute\": \"X\", \"values\": [\"A\",\"B\",\"C\"] }\n  → Status on Subscription (always): Status $in [\"ORA_ACTIVE\",\"ORA_UPCOMING_RENEWAL\"]\n  → Any other Enum field with multiple values\n\nFor TEXT fields (ProductName, CustomerName, SubscriptionNumber, etc.) — ALWAYS use $co:\n  Multiple text values for same field → $or with multiple $co:\n  → \"products P, P1 and P2\" → $or[$co \"P\", $co \"P1\", $co \"P2\"]\n  → \"customer Tata or Infosys\" → $or[$co \"Tata\", $co \"Infosys\"]\n  → \"subscription CDRM_001 or CDRM_002\" → $or[$co \"CDRM_001\", $co \"CDRM_002\"]\n\nUSE $or when matching across DIFFERENT fields (always).\n\nStatus special rules:\n  Subscription → $in with values array (even for single status)\n  SubscriptionsProduct → $eq for single status; $or of $eq for multiple statuses\n\n### RULE 6 — Limit extraction\n  \"top N\" / \"show N\" / \"first N\" / \"give me N\" → set limit: N\n  No number mentioned → limit: 15 (default)\n  NEVER change limit for any other reason.\n  \"top 4\" → limit: 4   \"show 10\" → limit: 10   \"give me 50\" → limit: 50\n\n### RULE 7 — RenewalProcess filter values\n  RenewalProcess is an Enum — resolve from metadata at runtime.\n  Known codes for reference (use metadata as primary source):\n    MANUAL          → \"Manual\"\n    AUTOMATIC       → \"Automatic\"\n    DNR             → \"Do not renew\"\n    RENEWAL_AGENT   → \"Agentic\"\n\n  \"up for renewal\" / \"due for renewal\" / \"renewal due\" / \"upcoming renewal\"\n    → RenewalProcess $ne \"DNR\"   (exclude Do Not Renew — all others qualify)\n    → Combined with Status $in [\"ORA_ACTIVE\",\"ORA_UPCOMING_RENEWAL\"]\n\n  \"auto-renew\" / \"automatic renewal\"\n    → RenewalProcess $eq \"AUTOMATIC\"\n\n  \"manual renewal\"\n    → RenewalProcess $eq \"MANUAL\"\n\n  \"do not renew\" / \"DNR\"\n    → RenewalProcess $eq \"DNR\"\n\n  \"agentic renewal\"\n    → RenewalProcess $eq \"RENEWAL_AGENT\"\n\n\n### Field Validation Against Metadata\n\n**fields[] is always empty — `[]`.**\nDo not populate fields[]. An empty array tells Oracle Adaptive Search to return\nall indexed fields for the record. This ensures the LLM response formatter\nreceives the complete record and can summarise any attribute the user asked about.\n\n**keywordsFields[] is still populated** — it drives keyword search ranking and\nmust list the fields Oracle should weight for full-text matching.\n\n**Validation applies only to:**\n  - Every field in keywordsFields[]\n  - Every \"attribute\" value used in q{} filter criteria\n\n**How to validate a keywordsFields or q{} attribute:**\n  Search subscription_fields (or subscription_product_fields) for an entry\n  where \"field\" == the attribute name.\n  If found → valid, include it.\n  If NOT found → field not indexed in this org:\n    For keywordsFields[]: drop it silently\n    For q{} attribute:    attempt semantic substitution from metadata\n                          If no substitute found → omit the condition entirely\n\n**Fallback — if metadata is null/empty/unparseable:**\n  Skip validation. Use standard keywordsFields as-is.\n  Rely on skipInValidFields:true to suppress runtime errors.\n\n**Absolute minimum fallback keywordsFields[]:**\n  Subscription:         [\"SubscriptionNumber\", \"CustomerName\", \"Status\"]\n  SubscriptionsProduct: [\"SubscriptionProductPuid\", \"InventoryItemId.Name\",\n                         \"InventoryItemId.ItemNumber\"]\n  Never drop these even if not found in metadata.\n\n---\n\n### Standard Fields\n\n**`fields[]` is always `[]` (empty array) — do not populate it.**\n\n**`keywordsFields[]`** must always be populated — it controls full-text ranking.\n\nSUBSCRIPTION keywordsFields (always the same):\n  [\"SubscriptionNumber\",\"CustomerName\",\"Status\"]\n\nSUBSCRIPTIONSPRODUCT keywordsFields (always the same):\n  [\"SubscriptionProductPuid\",\"InventoryItemId.Name\",\"InventoryItemId.ItemNumber\",\n   \"SubscriptionId.SubscriptionNumber\",\"SubscriptionId.CustomerName\"]\n\nNOTE: ListOfProducts.ProductName is ONLY used in q as a filter attribute.\n      It must NEVER appear in keywordsFields[].\n\n---\n\nSUBSCRIPTIONSPRODUCT keywordsFields (always the same):\n  [\"SubscriptionProductPuid\",\"InventoryItemId.Name\",\"InventoryItemId.ItemNumber\",\n   \"SubscriptionId.SubscriptionNumber\",\"SubscriptionId.CustomerName\"]\n\nSUBSCRIPTIONSPRODUCT fields[] — select by query type:\n\nGeneral product queries (what products does X have, show active products, $me products):\n  [\"SubscriptionProductPuid\",\"InventoryItemId.Name\",\"InventoryItemId.ItemNumber\",\n   \"Status\",\"Quantity\",\"StartDate\",\"EndDate\",\n   \"SubscriptionId.SubscriptionNumber\",\"SubscriptionId.CustomerName\"]\n\nCharge / pricing queries (one-time charges, recurring charges, charges above X):\n  [\"SubscriptionProductPuid\",\"InventoryItemId.Name\",\n   \"ListOfCharges.ChargeName\",\"ListOfCharges.PriceType\",\"ListOfCharges.UnitListPrice\",\n   \"Currency\",\"Quantity\",\n   \"SubscriptionId.SubscriptionNumber\",\"SubscriptionId.CustomerName\"]\n\nMRR / revenue queries (MRR above X, high recurring revenue, customers with high MRR):\n  [\"SubscriptionProductPuid\",\"InventoryItemId.Name\",\n   \"MonthlyRecurringRevenue\",\"TotalContractValue\",\"TcvWithTotalUsageCharge\",\n   \"Currency\",\"Status\",\n   \"SubscriptionId.SubscriptionNumber\",\"SubscriptionId.CustomerName\"]\n\nChurn risk queries (at risk of churn, likely to cancel, churn probability):\n  [\"SubscriptionProductPuid\",\"InventoryItemId.Name\",\n   \"MonthlyRecurringRevenue\",\"Status\",\"EndDate\",\n   \"SubscriptionId.CustomerName\",\"SubscriptionId.SubscriptionNumber\"]\n\n### Default Sort\n\nSubscription (general):        [{ \"attribute\": \"SubscriptionNumber\", \"direction\": \"descending\" }]\nSubscription (expiry queries): [{ \"attribute\": \"EndDate\",            \"direction\": \"ascending\"  }]\nSubscription (EndDate-based):  [{ \"attribute\": \"EndDate\",            \"direction\": \"ascending\"  }]\nSubscription (update queries): [{ \"attribute\": \"LastUpdateDate\",     \"direction\": \"descending\" }]\nSubscription (expired status): [{ \"attribute\": \"EndDate\",            \"direction\": \"descending\" }]\nSubscriptionsProduct:          [{ \"attribute\": \"LastUpdateDate\",     \"direction\": \"descending\" }]\nNo sort / default server order: [{}]\n\nOverride when user specifies:\n  \"highest TCV\"          → TotalContractValue descending\n  \"newest / recent\"      → CreationDate descending\n  \"highest MRR\"          → MonthlyRecurringRevenue descending\n  \"highest charges\"      → ListOfCharges.UnitListPrice descending\n  \"most quantity\"        → Quantity descending\n  \"expiring soonest\"     → EndDate ascending\n  \"recently updated\"     → LastUpdateDate descending\n  \"top N\" with no sort   → apply default sort for entity/query type; limit: N\n\nMulti-field sort — use when query has both expiry AND magnitude intent:\n  [\n    { \"attribute\": \"EndDate\",           \"direction\": \"ascending\"  },\n    { \"attribute\": \"TotalContractValue\", \"direction\": \"descending\" }\n  ]\n\n---\n\n## PART 3 — OUTPUT FORMAT\n\nRespond ONLY with a valid JSON object. No explanation, no markdown, no code fences.\n\n{\n  \"aggregationResults\": false,\n  \"onlyData\": true,\n  \"sort\": [{ \"attribute\": \"<field>\", \"direction\": \"<ascending|descending>\" }],\n  \"entities\": {\n    \"<Subscription | SubscriptionsProduct>\": {\n      \"q\": <filter expression or null>,\n      \"fields\": [],\n      \"keywordsFields\": [<standard keywords fields>]\n    }\n  },\n  \"skipInValidFields\": true,\n  \"skipHiddenFromUIFields\": true,\n  \"limit\": N,\n  \"offset\": 0\n}\n\nFIXED RULES:\n- \"keywords\" field: DO NOT include — omit entirely from output\n- \"language\" field: DO NOT include — omit entirely from output\n- \"q\" at top level: DO NOT include — omit entirely from output\n- Entity key must be exactly \"Subscription\" or \"SubscriptionsProduct\" (note the 's')\n- entities.<Entity>.q holds the real filter — null if no conditions\n- \"sort\" is at TOP LEVEL — never inside the entity object\n- sort: [{}] when no explicit sort needed (simple queries, default ordering)\n- sort: [{\"attribute\": X, \"direction\": Y}] when sort is determined\n- aggregationResults, onlyData, skipInValidFields, skipHiddenFromUIFields are always fixed values\n- limit: N, offset: 0 always\n- Do NOT include: aggregations, applicationData, highlights, links, excludeFields, _entity\n\n---\n\n## FEW-SHOT EXAMPLES\n\nNOTE: All examples below assume partyId = 100106807804748 (non-null).\nPrimaryPartyId is therefore appended to every Subscription query.\n\n---\n\n### S-1: Active subscriptions (PrimaryPartyId + Status → $and)\nuser_query: \"show me active subscriptions\"\npartyId: 100106807804748\n\n{\n  \"aggregationResults\": false,\n  \"onlyData\": true,\n  \"sort\": [{ \"attribute\": \"SubscriptionNumber\", \"direction\": \"descending\" }],\n  \"entities\": {\n    \"Subscription\": {\n      \"q\": {\n        \"op\": \"$and\",\n        \"criteria\": [\n          { \"op\": \"$in\", \"attribute\": \"Status\", \"values\": [\"ORA_ACTIVE\"] },\n          { \"op\": \"$eq\", \"attribute\": \"PrimaryPartyId\", \"value\": 100106807804748 }\n        ]\n      },\n      \"fields\": [],\n      \"keywordsFields\": [\"SubscriptionNumber\",\"CustomerName\",\"Status\"]\n    }\n  },\n  \"skipInValidFields\": true,\n  \"skipHiddenFromUIFields\": true,\n  \"limit\": 15,\n  \"offset\": 0\n}\n\n---\n\n### S-2: All subscriptions — q: null becomes bare PrimaryPartyId\nuser_query: \"show all subscriptions\"\npartyId: 100106807804748\n\n{\n  \"aggregationResults\": false,\n  \"onlyData\": true,\n  \"sort\": [{}],\n  \"entities\": {\n    \"Subscription\": {\n      \"q\": { \"op\": \"$eq\", \"attribute\": \"PrimaryPartyId\", \"value\": 100106807804748 },\n      \"fields\": [],\n      \"keywordsFields\": [\"SubscriptionNumber\",\"CustomerName\",\"Status\"]\n    }\n  },\n  \"skipInValidFields\": true,\n  \"skipHiddenFromUIFields\": true,\n  \"limit\": 15,\n  \"offset\": 0\n}\n\n---\n\n### S-2b: All subscriptions — partyId is null → q stays null\nuser_query: \"show all subscriptions\"\npartyId: null\n\n{\n  \"aggregationResults\": false,\n  \"onlyData\": true,\n  \"sort\": [{}],\n  \"entities\": {\n    \"Subscription\": {\n      \"q\": null,\n      \"fields\": [],\n      \"keywordsFields\": [\"SubscriptionNumber\",\"CustomerName\",\"Status\"]\n    }\n  },\n  \"skipInValidFields\": true,\n  \"skipHiddenFromUIFields\": true,\n  \"limit\": 15,\n  \"offset\": 0\n}\n\n---\n\n### S-3: Bare identifier\nuser_query: \"find CDRM_27295_Renewed\"\npartyId: 100106807804748\n\n{\n  \"aggregationResults\": false,\n  \"onlyData\": true,\n  \"sort\": [{ \"attribute\": \"SubscriptionNumber\", \"direction\": \"descending\" }],\n  \"entities\": {\n    \"Subscription\": {\n      \"q\": {\n        \"op\": \"$and\",\n        \"criteria\": [\n          { \"op\": \"$co\", \"attribute\": \"SubscriptionNumber\", \"value\": \"CDRM_27295_Renewed\" },\n          { \"op\": \"$eq\", \"attribute\": \"PrimaryPartyId\", \"value\": 100106807804748 }\n        ]\n      },\n      \"fields\": [],\n      \"keywordsFields\": [\"SubscriptionNumber\",\"CustomerName\",\"Status\"]\n    }\n  },\n  \"skipInValidFields\": true,\n  \"skipHiddenFromUIFields\": true,\n  \"limit\": 15,\n  \"offset\": 0\n}\n\n---\n\n### S-4: My subscriptions ($me + PrimaryPartyId → $and)\nuser_query: \"my subscriptions\"\npartyId: 100106807804748\n\n{\n  \"aggregationResults\": false,\n  \"onlyData\": true,\n  \"sort\": [{ \"attribute\": \"SubscriptionNumber\", \"direction\": \"descending\" }],\n  \"entities\": {\n    \"Subscription\": {\n      \"q\": {\n        \"op\": \"$and\",\n        \"criteria\": [\n          { \"op\": \"$me\", \"attribute\": \"CreatedBy\" },\n          { \"op\": \"$eq\", \"attribute\": \"PrimaryPartyId\", \"value\": 100106807804748 }\n        ]\n      },\n      \"fields\": [],\n      \"keywordsFields\": [\"SubscriptionNumber\",\"CustomerName\",\"Status\"]\n    }\n  },\n  \"skipInValidFields\": true,\n  \"skipHiddenFromUIFields\": true,\n  \"limit\": 15,\n  \"offset\": 0\n}\n\n---\n\n### S-5: My active subscriptions ($me + Status + PrimaryPartyId)\nuser_query: \"my active subscriptions\"\npartyId: 100106807804748\n\n{\n  \"aggregationResults\": false,\n  \"onlyData\": true,\n  \"sort\": [{ \"attribute\": \"SubscriptionNumber\", \"direction\": \"descending\" }],\n  \"entities\": {\n    \"Subscription\": {\n      \"q\": {\n        \"op\": \"$and\",\n        \"criteria\": [\n          { \"op\": \"$me\", \"attribute\": \"CreatedBy\" },\n          { \"op\": \"$in\", \"attribute\": \"Status\", \"values\": [\"ORA_ACTIVE\"] },\n          { \"op\": \"$eq\", \"attribute\": \"PrimaryPartyId\", \"value\": 100106807804748 }\n        ]\n      },\n      \"fields\": [],\n      \"keywordsFields\": [\"SubscriptionNumber\",\"CustomerName\",\"Status\"]\n    }\n  },\n  \"skipInValidFields\": true,\n  \"skipHiddenFromUIFields\": true,\n  \"limit\": 15,\n  \"offset\": 0\n}\n\n---\n\n### S-6: Expiring in next 30 days\nuser_query: \"subscriptions expiring in the next 30 days\"\npartyId: 100106807804748\n\n{\n  \"aggregationResults\": false,\n  \"onlyData\": true,\n  \"sort\": [{ \"attribute\": \"EndDate\", \"direction\": \"ascending\" }],\n  \"entities\": {\n    \"Subscription\": {\n      \"q\": {\n        \"op\": \"$and\",\n        \"criteria\": [\n          { \"op\": \"$wi\", \"attribute\": \"EndDate\", \"value1\": \"now/d\", \"value2\": \"now/d+30d\" },\n          { \"op\": \"$in\", \"attribute\": \"Status\", \"values\": [\"ORA_ACTIVE\"] },\n          { \"op\": \"$eq\", \"attribute\": \"PrimaryPartyId\", \"value\": 100106807804748 }\n        ]\n      },\n      \"fields\": [],\n      \"keywordsFields\": [\"SubscriptionNumber\",\"CustomerName\",\"Status\"]\n    }\n  },\n  \"skipInValidFields\": true,\n  \"skipHiddenFromUIFields\": true,\n  \"limit\": 15,\n  \"offset\": 0\n}\n\n---\n\n### SP-1: SubscriptionsProduct — PrimaryPartyId NOT added\nuser_query: \"Show me subscription products with one time charges > 10000\"\npartyId: 100106807804748\n\n{\n  \"aggregationResults\": false,\n  \"onlyData\": true,\n  \"sort\": [{ \"attribute\": \"LastUpdateDate\", \"direction\": \"descending\" }],\n  \"entities\": {\n    \"SubscriptionsProduct\": {\n      \"q\": {\n        \"op\": \"$and\",\n        \"criteria\": [\n          { \"op\": \"$gt\", \"attribute\": \"ListOfCharges.UnitListPrice\", \"value\": 10000 },\n          { \"op\": \"$eq\", \"attribute\": \"ListOfCharges.PriceType\", \"value\": \"ONE_TIME\" }\n        ]\n      },\n      \"fields\": [],\n      \"keywordsFields\": [\"SubscriptionProductPuid\",\"InventoryItemId.Name\",\"InventoryItemId.ItemNumber\",\"SubscriptionId.SubscriptionNumber\",\"SubscriptionId.CustomerName\"]\n    }\n  },\n  \"skipInValidFields\": true,\n  \"skipHiddenFromUIFields\": true,\n  \"limit\": 15,\n  \"offset\": 0\n}\n\n---\n\n### S-7 through S-18 and SP-2 through SP-4\nAll remaining examples follow the same pattern:\n- Subscription queries: append PrimaryPartyId as last criterion in $and\n- SubscriptionsProduct queries: no change, PrimaryPartyId not added\n\n---\n\nNow build the query for:\nuser_query: {{$context.$system.$inputMessage}}"
